version: v1alpha1
metadata:
  name: nfs-server
  version: "{{ .VERSION }}"
  author: Mateusz Urbanek
  description: |
    [{{ .TIER }}] This system extension provides the nfs-utils server-side daemons, turning
    the node into an NFS server serving NFSv3, v4.0, v4.1 and v4.2.

    exportfs syncs the kernel export table from /etc/exports.
    rpc.mountd services NFSv3 mount requests and the kernel's export upcalls.
    nfsdcld tracks NFSv4 clients so they can reclaim state after a server restart.
    rpc.nfsd starts the kernel NFS server threads.

    Requires the nfsd kernel module from the `nfsd` extension, and the `nfs-utils`
    extension for rpcbind and rpc.statd.
  compatibility:
    talos:
      version: ">= v1.14.0"
